From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thuong Vo <66083331+SekiroKenjii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: compile the Apex resource into gnome-control-center

The Apex Settings ship inside gnome-control-center. Their sources come
from Source1, a git archive of desktop/control-center/ in apex-gnome,
which %prep unpacks at the top of this tree as panels/apex/.
panels/meson.build reads panels/apex/meson.build after upstream's panels,
and shell/meson.build compiles the sources it gives, the Apex resource
/org/gnome/Settings/apex, straight into gnome-control-center: as
sources, not a static library, so the linker keeps them while no
upstream code calls them. Nothing loads the resource yet.
---
 panels/meson.build | 1 +
 shell/meson.build  | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/panels/meson.build b/panels/meson.build
index 07c7733..8987c3a 100644
--- a/panels/meson.build
+++ b/panels/meson.build
@@ -46,3 +46,4 @@ foreach cappletname: dependent_panels + panels
 
   subdir(cappletname)
 endforeach
+subdir('apex')
diff --git a/shell/meson.build b/shell/meson.build
index 79405f9..892dc38 100644
--- a/shell/meson.build
+++ b/shell/meson.build
@@ -112,6 +112,7 @@ libshell_dep = declare_dependency(
 ########################
 
 shell_sources = common_sources + files('main.c')
+shell_sources += apex_shell_sources
 
 shell_deps = common_deps + [
   libdevice_dep,
